# AntennaTracker defaults for the camera towers.
#
# PITCH_MIN/PITCH_MAX must match the tilt joint limits in terrain/tower.py.
# ArduPilot maps its full servo range onto this span, and the Gazebo plugin
# maps that same servo range onto the joint range -- so if the two disagree the
# tracker either cannot reach its limits or grinds against a hard stop.
#
# Positive pitch is up in ArduPilot; the joint's positive direction is down.
#
# -30, not -70. SCAN sweeps the WHOLE PITCH_MIN..PITCH_MAX span, so every
# degree of downward travel is time spent staring at the ground: at -70 that
# was 61% of each sweep below the horizon.
#
# -30 is chosen from the actual site geometry, not taste. Both towers stand
# well above what they watch (camera at 118 m and 230 m; the vessel is at sea
# level and aircraft cruise near 60 m), so some down-look is essential -- this
# is NOT a case where the horizon is the natural floor:
#
#   vessel, from either tower          ~5 deg down
#   aircraft at 60 m, from tower-2     9.6 deg at 1 km, 19 deg at 500 m,
#                                      30 deg at 300 m horizontal
#
# So -30 still reaches everything down to roughly 300 m horizontal from the
# higher tower. Below that the target is very close and passing quickly.
# Clamping harder (-10, say) would look tidy on a scan and lose aircraft
# tracking altogether.
#
# CHANGING THIS MEANS CHANGING THREE THINGS. The joint <limit> and the tilt
# <control> mapping in terrain/tower.py are derived from these numbers; edit
# one alone and the servo range stops landing on the joint range.
PITCH_MIN -30
PITCH_MAX 45
YAW_RANGE 360

# SITL has no calibrated accels or compass, so the stock prearm set can never
# pass. A tower has no propulsion to make safe.
ARMING_CHECK 0

# Boot into MANUAL, not AUTO.
#
# AUTO with no tracked vehicle emits PWM 0 on both channels. SIM_Gazebo
# normalises PWM as (pwm-1000)/1000, so 0 becomes a command of -1.0, and the
# plugin's target = multiplier*(offset+cmd) then lands far outside the joint
# range. The position loop grinds against the hard stop and the whole head
# buzzes. MANUAL holds 1500/1500 -- pan centred, tilt mid-range -- and takes
# pan/tilt commands over MAVLink, which is what a camera tower wants anyway.
# Switch to AUTO from a GCS once there is a vehicle to track.
INITIAL_MODE 0
